{PDOC00228}
{PS00255; INTERLEUKIN_7_9}
{BEGIN}
**********************************
* Interleukin-7 and -9 signature *
**********************************

Interleukin-7 (IL-7) [1] is  a  cytokine  that  serves as a  growth factor for
early lymphoid  cells of both B- and T-cell lineages. Interleukin-9 (IL-9) [2]
is a  cytokine  that  supports IL-2 independent and IL-4 independent growth of
helper T-cells.

Interleukin-7 and  -9  seems  to  be  evolutionary related [3]. As a signature
pattern, we  selected  a conserved region located in the C-terminal section of
the protein.

-Consensus pattern: N-x-[LAP]-[SCT]-F-L-K-x-L-L
-Sequences known to belong to this class detected by the pattern: ALL.
-Other sequence(s) detected in Swiss-Prot: NONE.

