{PDOC00778}
{PS01015; RIBOSOMAL_L19}
{BEGIN}
***********************************
* Ribosomal protein L19 signature *
***********************************

Ribosomal protein L19 is one of the proteins from the large ribosomal subunit.
In Escherichia  coli,  L19  is  known  to  be located at the 30S-50S ribosomal
subunit interface  and  may  play  a role in the structure and function of the
aminoacyl-tRNA  binding site.  It  belongs  to a  family of ribosomal proteins
which, on the basis of sequence similarities, groups:

 - Eubacterial L19.
 - Red algal chloroplast L19.
 - Cyanelle L19.

L19 is  a  protein of 120 to 130 amino-acid residues.  As a signature pattern,
we selected a conserved region in the C-terminal section.

-Consensus pattern: [LIVMF]-x-[KRGTIEQSN]-x-[GSAIYN]-[KRQDAVLSIH]-[VGAIT]-
                    [RSNAK]-x(0,1)-[KRAQ]-[SAKG]-[KYR]-[KLI]-[LYSFT]-[YF]-
                    [LIM]-[RK]
-Sequences known to belong to this class detected by the pattern: ALL.
-Other sequence(s) detected in Swiss-Prot: NONE.
-Last update: April 2006 / Pattern revised.
{END}
{PDOC00779}
{PS01016; GLYCOPROTEASE}
{BEGIN}
**********************************
* Glycoprotease family signature *
**********************************

Glycoprotease (GCP)  (EC 3.4.24.57) [1], or o-syaloglycoprotein endopeptidase,
is a  metalloprotease  secreted  by Pasteurella haemolytica which specifically
cleaves O-sialoglycoproteins  such  as glycophorin A.  The  sequence of GCP is
highly similar  to  uncharacterized  orthologs  in  most  complete  genomes of
bacteria and archaebacteria as well as in yeast (QRI7 and YKR038c).

One of the conserved regions contains two conserved histidines. It is possible
that this region is involved in coordinating a metal ion such as zinc.

-Consensus pattern: [KRC]-[GSAT]-x(4)-[FYWLMH]-[DQNGKRH]-x-P-x-[LIVMFY]-x(3)-
                    H-x(2)-[GSA]-H-[LIVMFA]
                    [The 2 H's may be zinc ligands]
-Sequences known to belong to this class detected by the pattern: ALL.
-Other sequence(s) detected in Swiss-Prot: NONE.

-Note: These proteins belong to family M22 in the classification of peptidases
 [2,E1].

