     Loison G., Jacobsson A.
     "Role of a new mammalian gene family in the biosynthesis of very long
     chain fatty acids and sphingolipids."
     J. Cell Biol. 149:707-718(2000).
     PubMed=10791983
[ 2] Oh C.-S., Toke D.A., Mandala S., Martin C.E.
     "ELO2 and ELO3, homologues of the Saccharomyces cerevisiae ELO1 gene,
     function in fatty acid elongation and are required for sphingolipid
     formation."
     J. Biol. Chem. 272:17376-17384(1997).
