{PS01262; IF1A}
{BEGIN}
*********************************************
* Eukaryotic initiation factor 1A signature *
*********************************************

Eukaryotic translation  initiation  factor  1A (eIF-1A) [1] (formerly known as
eiF-4C) is a protein that seems to  be  required  for  maximal rate of protein
biosynthesis. It  enhances  ribosome dissociation into subunits and stabilizes
the binding of the initiator Met-tRNA to 40S ribosomal subunits.

eIF-1A is a hydrophilic protein of about 15 to 17 Kd. Archaebacteria also seem
to possess a eIF-1A homolog.

As a  signature pattern, we selected a conserved region in the central section
of these proteins.

-Consensus pattern: [IMVALH]-x-G-x-[GSDENK]-[KRHFW]-x(4)-[CL]-x-D-G-x(2)-[RY]-
                    x(2)-[RH]-[IL]-x-G
-Sequences known to belong to this class detected by the pattern: ALL.
