{BEGIN}
*************************************
* Enhancer of rudimentary signature *
*************************************

The Drosophila  protein  'enhancer  of  rudimentary'  (gene  (e(r)) is a small
protein of  104 residues whose function is not yet clear. From an evolutionary
point of  view,  it  is  highly  conserved  [1] and has been found to exist in
probably all  multicellular  eukaryotic  organisms.  It has been proposed that
this protein plays a role in the cell cycle.

As as  signaure pattern, we selected a conserved region in the central part of
the protein.

