{PDOC50244}
{PS50244; S5A_REDUCTASE}
{BEGIN}
*******************************************************
* Steroid 5-alpha reductase C-terminal domain profile *
*******************************************************

Steroid 5-alpha  reductases  (EC  1.3.99.5)  are  responsible  for  the NADPH-
dependent reduction  of  testosterone into dihydrotestosterone, a key reaction
in androgen action [1]. This enzyme  is  also  found  in  plants  where  it is
involved in    brassinosteroids  biosynthesis [2]. A domain of around 80 amino
acids is  found in the C-terminal part of the protein and contains the binding
site for NADPH [3].

