{PDOC51019}
{PS51019; REELIN}
{BEGIN}
*************************
* Reelin domain profile *
*************************

The reelin  domain  is  a ~170 amino acid module, which has been identified in
the amino  terminus  of the extracellular matrix proteins reelin and F-spondin
(renamed Spon1).  The  spondin  domain  is  found  in  association  with other
modules, such  as  the  thrombospondin type I repeat (TSP1) (see <PDOC50092>),
the spondin  domain  (see  <PDOC51020>),  the fibronectin type III domain (see
<PDOC50853>) or   the   Kunitz   trypsin   protease   inhibitor   domain  (see
<PDOC00252>). The function of the reelin domain is not yet known [1,2,3].

The profile we developed covers the entire reelin domain.

