{PDOC51756}
{PS51756; LXG}
{BEGIN}
**********************
* LXG domain profile *
**********************

The bacterial  LXG  domain contains a conserved [LF]-X-G sequence motif and is
predicted to assume an alpha-helical bundle fold. The LXG is predicted to be a
secretion signal  for  the  type  VII  secretion  system  of Mycobacterium and
Bacillus species. It is likely to utilize the ATP-dependent YueA pumps and the
potential peptide-binding  EsaC  domain  as  partners  for  extrusion from the
producing cell [1,2].

The profile we developed covers the entire LXG domain.

