{PDOC51804}
{PS51804; ZF_C2HC_LYAR}
{BEGIN}
**************************************
* Zinc finger C2HC LYAR-type profile *
**************************************

Zinc finger  (ZF)  proteins are a large family of metalloproteins that utilize
zinc for  structural  purposes.  Zinc coordinates to a combination of cysteine
thiol and  histidine  imidazole  residues  within  the  ZF polypetide sequence
resulting in  a  folded  and  functional protein. Ly-1 antibody reactive clone
(Lyar), which  is  known  to  be expressed abundantly in the testis, encodes a
nucleolar protein  that  contain  a LYAR-type C2HC zinc finger motif and three
nuclear localization  signals.  It is a nucleolar protein abundantly expressed
in spermatocytes  and spermatids, but not sperm. LYAR forms a complex with the
nucleolin, which  is  one  of  the  most  abundant  proteins  in the nucleolus
[1,2,3].

The profile we developed covers the entire LYAR-type C2HC zinc finger.

