     Eur. J. Biochem. 271:1135-1144(2004).
     PubMed=15009192
{END}
{PDOC51817}
{PS51817; PEPTIDASE_A3B}
{BEGIN}
***************************************
* Peptidase family A3B domain profile *
***************************************

Rice tungro  bacilliform virus (RTBV) is a pararetrovirus, and a member of the
family Caulimoviridae  in  the  genus  Tungrovirus  [E1]. RTBV has a long open
reading frame  that  encodes  a large polyprotein (P3). P3 contains a putative
movement protein  (MP),  the  capsid protein (CP), the aspartate protease (PR)
and the  reverse  transcriptase  (RT)  with a ribonuclease H activity. PR is a
member of  the  cluster  of retroviral proteases and serves to proteolytically
process P3.  The sequence DSGS is believed to be the RTBV protease active site
[1]. The RTBV PR domain forms peptidase family A3 subfamily B [E2].

The profile we developed covers the entire peptidase family A3B domain.

