{PDOC52085}
{PS52085; HERC2_LIKE}
{BEGIN}
*****************************
* HERC2-like domain profile *
*****************************

The HERC2-like  domain,  also  called HERC2-like repeat, HERC2-related repeat,
Mib repeat,  Mib-like  repeat  or  iron-sulfur cluster-dependent NCOA4-binding
domain (INBD), is found in one to nine copies in the following proteins:

 - Animal  HERC2,  an E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase which accepts ubiquitin from
   an E2  ubiquitin-conjugating  enzyme  in  the  form of a thioester and then
   directly transfers  the ubiquitin to targeted substrates. HERC2 consists of
   three regulator  of chromosome condensation 1-like domains (RLDs) each made
   of seven  RCC1  repeats  (see  <PDOC00544>),  a cytochrome-b5 like (cyt-b5)
   domain (see <PDOC00170>), a MIB/HERC2 domain (see <PDOC51416>), a Cullin-7-
   PARC-HERC2 (CPH)  domain  (see <PDOC52081>), a HERC2-like domain, a ZZ-type
   zinc finger  (ZZ)  domain  (see  <PDOC50135>),  a down regulated in ovarian
   cancer (DOC)  domain  (see  <PDOC51284>),  and  a  C-terminal catalytic E3-
   enzymatic homologous  to  E6AP  C-terminus  (HECT) domain (see <PDOC50237>)
   [1].
 - Animal Mind bomb (Mib) proteins, large multi-domain E3 ligases that promote
   ubiquitination of  the  cytoplasmic  tails of Notch ligands. In addition to
   their role   as  Notch  ligand  effectors,  Mib  proteins  have  also  been
   implicated as  ubiquitin  ligases for proteins involved in innate immunity,
   neuronal function,  Wnt/beta-catenin signaling, genomic stability, and cell
   death. Mib proteins are made of four contiguous structural elements: (i) an
   MZM region, which contains two Mib-Herc2 domains (see <PDOC51416>) flanking
   a ZZ  zinc finger (ZZ) (see <PDOC50135>); (ii) a REP region, which includes
   two tandem  repeats of HERC2-like domains; (iii) an ANK region, which spans
   nine ankyrin  (ANK) repeats (see <PDOC50088>); and (iv) a RNG region, which
   contains two or three RING fingers (see (<PDOC00449>) [2].
 - Arabidopsis thaliana KEG (for KEEP ON GOING), a RING E3 ligase required for
   abscisic acid  (ABA)  signaling and postgerminative growth of seedlings. It
   contains a   RING   finger   (see   <PDOC00449>),   a  kinase  domain  (see
   <PDOC00100>), nine  ANK  repeats  (see  <PDOC50088>)  and twelve HERC2-like
   repeats [3,4].
 - Arabidopsis  thaliana  KOC1, an integral chloroplast envelope kinase acting
   as a  regulatory  component  of  the  plastid  protein  import machinery by
   phosphorylating import  receptors  (e.g. the A-domain of TOC159, TOC120 and
   TOC132). KOC1  contains  a kinase domain (see <PDOC00100>), a HERC2-related
   region made  of  two HERC2-like domains and a predicted transmembrane helix
   [5].

HERC2-like domains have been shown to mediate a large range of protein:protein
interactions [1,2,3,4].

The HERC2-like  domain  folds  have a five-stranded anti-parallel twisted beta
sheet topology  similar  to  that of SH3 domains, even though the two types of
modules have no detectable sequence homology (see <PDB:4XI6>) [1,2].

The profile we developed covers the entire HERC2-like domain.

-Sequences known to belong to this class detected by the profile: ALL.
-Other sequence(s) detected in Swiss-Prot: NONE.
